// What the model gives, written by `BLESS=1` (design/19-cases.md).
run 1: Readings { visibility: ByMember, binding_path: AsStated, deferral: Recording }, every order
outcome 1
  refused
  value ?a: u16
  value R: u16
  value X: u16
  value `m(x)`: ()
  value `n(x)`: ()
  decision id: id#0
  decision m: m#0
  decision n: n#1
  partition {?a, R, X}
  check `?a <= X`: Ok(Identity)
  check `R <= X`: Ok(Identity)
  check `X <= id.Var(Type(0))`: Ok(Identity)
  check `X ~> m.Param(0)`: Ok(Identity)
  check `X ~> n.Param(0)`: Err(None)
  check `id.Var(Type(0)) <= R`: Ok(Identity)
  check `m.Result <= m(x)`: Ok(Identity)
  check `n.Result <= n(x)`: Ok(Identity)
  refusal conflict at "X = n.Param(0)": Scalar(Int(U16)) vs Scalar(Int(I32))
  I* of a final state: [completeness m, completeness n]
